ve a short summary  the new chapter of the european  pharmacopoeia deals with balances for  analytical purposes  it became mandatory on the 1st of  january this year  and affects pharmaceutical companies  manufacturing drugs for the european  market  so this new regulation does not only  affect companies located within the  european union  but manufacturing drugs for the european  union  the new chapter focuses on best  practices for installation and usage of  instruments and highlights the  importance of calibrations and the  documentation a certificate including  the measurement uncertainty  and supports the life science management  of instruments based on the performed  tests and calibrations  the european pharmacopoeia chapter 2.1.7  lists a lot of general considerations  for analytical balances like for example  it defines the si units as force is mass  multiplied by gravity  it defines a balanced side mechanical  electronical and the resolution  and it deals with installation and  location  the new chapter gives clear guidance how  to monitor environmental conditions at  the insulation side  like temperature  humidity and barometric pressure  and gives recommendations how to avoid  air carbons  dust electrostatic forces magnetic  forces and  vibrations to deal with these topics  satorius offers different technical  solutions and these are mentioned in  brackets on the slide  to measure environmental conditions and  the installation side we offer climate  modules and a software for air buoyancy  correction  to avoid air currents and dust special  glass trees weighing pen or covers can  be used  for the elimination of electrostatic  forces and magnetic forces ionizers and  antimagnetic weighing plants are  available  and to avoid vibrations weighing tables  can be used  in addition to these general  considerations  chapter  2.1.7 also deals with the equipment  performance  in detail about calibrations and  performance checks  regarding the performance checks the