n be used  the software application allows to  conduct a performance check according to  usp or the european pharmacopoeia  and it displays recommendations for the  test loads  if the european pharmacopoeia is  selected  the software application offers a guided  workflow for the sensitivity and  repeatability test  in combination with the compatibility  check of the determined minimum sample  weight  at the end of the test the user gets an  information displayed if they calculate  a minimum sample weight complies to the  requirements  the screen additionally offers to set  the minimum sample weight that is then  used by the software application minimum  weight  as discussed before the software  application minimum weight can control  that no sample weights below the  permissible minimum weight  are acquired  before i will give a final summary just  a few words on the minimal sample weight  and its usage in the pharmaceutical  industry  according to usp and the european  pharmacopoeia it is forbidden to acquire  sample weights below the minimum weight  so in best case 820 multiplied by the  scale interval  the effective minimum sample weight for  balance depends on the environment so  the installation side and the ambient  conditions  it's important to know that by  definition the minimum sample weight  refers to net values so using a high  tear weight does not lead to a higher  permissible minimum sample weight  instead the balance sensitivity must be  high enough and the balance must be  installed under good conditions to offer  a low minimum sample weight  using vessels with high tear weight is  not a solution and in worst case the fda  issues warning letters if usb chapter 41  is violated  in summary the european pharmacopoeia  chapter 2.1.7  defines the general requirements for  analytical balances used in the  pharmaceutical industry  the minimum weight is defined like an  usb 820 digits or higher  it provides clear guidance on test loads  used for the repeatability and  sensitivity test  and it has a tighter requirement on the  systematic errors in the usp  0.05 percent versus 0.1 percent  to maintain compliance  sartorius modified the queue app's  minimum weight and usp advanced  according to the european pharmacopoeia  chapter 2.1.7  in the software application minimum  weight the user can select between  different guidelines now and a check for  820 digits has been implemented to the  software application usb advanced a  performance check procedure according to  the european pharmacopoeia has been  added  the software application checks if the  determined value for the minimum sample  weight complies with usp  of european pharmacopoeia requirements  if the value is compliant it can be set  by the software and used by the software  application minimum weight  to prevent the acquisition of weight  values below the minimum sample rate  thank you very much for joining our  presentation today i hope we gave you  some new insights into the topic of  compliance for laboratory balances  please feel free to ask us if you have  any questions or visit our website  if you want to have more information  about the presented instruments  thank you dr denzo for your informative  presentation  we will now start the live q a portion  of the webinar  if you have a question you'd like to ask  please do so now just click on the ask a  question box located on the far left of  your screen we'll answer as many of your  questions as we have time for  all right let's get started our first  question here asks do i have to  administrate users at the balance or can  i connect the balance to out ldap server  that's a great question  well um of course you can administrate  users at the balance but if you own many  balances and you're working in a larger  company or a larger lab and it gets  cumbersome  yeah  administrate all users on all balances  so  yes the answer is you can hook up the  balance to your local ldap server  and  then easy users are